# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Keeping the context small makes builds faster, but the important job here
# is correctness: nothing that represents RUNTIME STATE may be baked into the
# image. State belongs in the mounted volume, not in the artifact.

# --- Version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Python bytecode and caches --------------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache

# --- Virtual environments --------------------------------------------------
venv
env
.venv

# --- Runtime state: MUST NOT be baked into the image -----------------------
# The SQLite database is runtime state. If a copy were baked in, a rebuilt
# container could start from a stale database and silently lose feedback, or
# ship one developer's data to everyone.
database
database/*.db
*.db
*.sqlite3

# --- Pipeline scratch space ------------------------------------------------
# build/ holds the candidate model between Jenkins stages. A candidate has
# NOT passed the quality gate, so it must never reach a deployable image.
build

# --- Test evidence ---------------------------------------------------------
selenium_tests/screenshots
selenium_tests/screenshots/*.png

# --- Editor and OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# --- Documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
docs
*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY *NOT* EXCLUDED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   models/*.pkl    The staged production model. Jenkins copies it here from
#                   the persistent store immediately before the build, and
#                   baking it in is the entire point of the deployment
#                   approach from the ML deployment practical: the image is a
#                   self-contained artifact holding both the code and the
#                   exact model it serves.
#
#   data/*.csv      The training pool and the frozen holdout set. Small, and
#                   they keep the image able to retrain or re-evaluate.
#
#   tests/          Small, and lets the suite be run inside the container to
#                   confirm the built image is sound.
